# "The value of X is determined as Chain Reaction resolves" (CR 608.2): three creatures are on the battlefield when it is
# cast - the Hill Giant, Bot1's Ornithopter and Bot2's Ornithopter - and Bot2 answers with Shatter on its own Ornithopter,
# leaving two. X is therefore 2, not 3: the 3/3 Hill Giant takes 2 and survives, while its Ornithopter dies. Had the count
# been fixed at casting, the Giant would take 3 and die (and the Ornithopter's own 2 would not be dealt at all).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Hill Giant
Chain Reaction
Ornithopter
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Shatter
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Hill Giant.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Chain Reaction.Cast
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Shatter.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Hill Giant.Damage = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Hill Giant.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter = (absent)
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 4
Bot2.Graveyard = Shatter; Ornithopter
